#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ABOUTME: Retired front door for the old SFR Box NAT manager; the site now runs a Livebox.
# ABOUTME: Refuses rather than retargets — the two CLIs take different argument orders.
#
# The workstation moved 2026-08-06 and the SFR NB6VAC stayed behind. This
# wrapper drove nat_manager/nat.py, which speaks the NB6VAC's challenge-response
# API and cannot talk to a Livebox at all.
#
# It refuses instead of silently forwarding to the new tool on purpose: the
# argument orders differ (this took `<name> <ext> <last-octet> <int>`, the
# Livebox CLI takes `<name> <external> <target_ip> [internal]`), so a silent
# retarget would quietly create WRONG rules rather than fail.
set -euo pipefail

cat >&2 <<'MSG'
open-port is retired: this site's gateway is a Livebox, not an SFR Box.

Use the current adapter instead:

  ~/42/GroundControl/network/routers/livebox list
  ~/42/GroundControl/network/routers/livebox add <name> <external> <target_ip> [internal] [--protocol tcp|udp]
  ~/42/GroundControl/network/routers/livebox delete <name>

It fetches the router password from Proton Pass per invocation; there is no
SFR_BOX_PASSWORD and no ~/.secrets.sh step any more.

Site truth (gateway, LAN, live rules): GroundControl network/sites/.
MSG
exit 2
